import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Principles" description="Consistency, Modularity, Circumnavigability — Cleo Design System">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Principles</h1>
    <hr class="section-accent-rule" />
    <p class="page-lead">
      Three core values govern every token, component, and block. Return here when scope
      creeps or a screen feels off-brand.
    </p>

    <h2>Consistency</h2>
    <p>
      Everything looks and behaves the same way because it pulls from the same token spine,
      voice rules, and geometry — not one-off choices per screen. Amber appears once per
      view. No pure black or white. Denial UI is a guardian, not an alarm.
    </p>

    <h2>Modularity</h2>
    <p>
      Build with small, reusable pieces that snap together like Lego: tokens → components →
      blocks → patterns. Julie's kit ships first; later clinics add or swap modules without
      rewriting the whole app. Each block has bounded interfaces — not a hospital tab forest.
    </p>

    <h2>Circumnavigability</h2>
    <p>
      Anyone can find where they are, get to what they need in a few clicks, and move forward
      or back without feeling lost. In product: river geometry — calm forward motion, Patients
      and profile as escape hatches. In this site: registry hub, related links, clear nav.
    </p>

    <h2>Quiet Authority</h2>
    <p>
      Confidence without shouting. Warmth without performance. The interface steps back as work
      completes. Lora for authority at scale; DM Sans for UI. Motion fades and settles — never
      bounce or confetti.
    </p>

    <h2>Closed workflow geometry</h2>
    <p>Five rules from Julie MVP closed geometry (visit shell, not flat EMR):</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>One visit shell</strong> — everything for the visit lives in one place</li>
      <li><strong>One primary forward CTA</strong> per screen</li>
      <li><strong>Poles visible</strong> — status strip shows where you are in the arc</li>
      <li><strong>Circumnavigable tabs</strong> — jump without leaving the visit</li>
      <li><strong>Human accepts AI</strong> — suggestions are HITL, never silent auto-apply</li>
    </ol>

    <p>
      See <a href="/blocks/visit-shell">Visit shell block</a> and
      <a href="/registry">Registry</a> for implementation.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
